{"title":"2013 Indonesia MO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9b84c9767d548714b9f1c08d04298f1382eb2f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> grid, all edges and diagonals are drawn (see attachment). Determine the number of parallelograms in the grid that uses only the line segments drawn and none of its four angles are right.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/10995b3045df9ed5f8cefb255abf401711d562ee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(6,0)--(6,4)--(0,4)--(0,0)); for (int i=1; i&lt;6; ++i) { draw((i,0)--(i,4)); } for (int i=1; i&lt;4; ++i) { draw((0,i)--(6,i)); } draw((0,1)--(1,0)); draw((0,2)--(2,0)); draw((0,3)--(3,0)); draw((0,4)--(4,0)); draw((1,4)--(5,0)); draw((2,4)--(6,0)); draw((3,4)--(6,1)); draw((4,4)--(6,2)); draw((5,4)--(6,3)); draw((0,3)--(1,4)); draw((0,2)--(2,4)); draw((0,1)--(3,4)); draw((0,0)--(4,4)); draw((1,0)--(5,4)); draw((2,0)--(6,4)); draw((3,0)--(6,3)); draw((4,0)--(6,2)); draw((5,0)--(6,1));   [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"168\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be an acute triangle and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> be its circumcircle. The bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> at [another point] <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> and inside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Lines passing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> that are parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/3/033ff41b019f4360f1312fc129c262d1050e63c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E, F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> respectively. Lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/d/33d5b8a976539db40d4a3491086a1eec310bdb4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ME, MF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/7/8574f36470fbc7b0993b3173981a8cf08b597bd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K, L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> respectively. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/9/e4976718c48be382a2b0e965b1be12ed106b9784.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM, BL, CK$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" /> are concurrent.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Determine all positive real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> such that for any positive reals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />, at least one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c419b042a8eeefcf7f1ec385d4c0fc23c452505.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + \\dfrac{M}{ab}, b + \\dfrac{M}{bc}, c + \\dfrac{M}{ca}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"177\" height=\"37\" /> is greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acd0d2d82d5acdd6da98043e23c2891a6f349e2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/3/8437e1b1294378b7f0a667ffc66215648662ec71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p &gt; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> is a prime number and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/b/a3b8f0ef8c437e7ee236fb9b5b8f3ffbacf93c2a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S = \\sum_{2 \\le i &lt; j &lt; k \\le p-1} ijk\\]\" width=\"153\" height=\"40\" />\nProve that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/0/8f0cd31d4f9286e15e327c22a45269273c01b1e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a quadratic (polynomial of degree two) with a positive leading coefficient and negative discriminant. Prove that there exists three quadratics <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fd628c2338dc339d3e6a10257752d208924b1eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1, P_2, P_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> such that:\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/2/782014c34705c55ebcb06b28ddebee6a32a85eac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = P_1(x) + P_2(x) + P_3(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"237\" height=\"18\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fd628c2338dc339d3e6a10257752d208924b1eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1, P_2, P_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> have positive leading coefficients and zero discriminants (and hence each has a double root)</li>\n<li>The roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fd628c2338dc339d3e6a10257752d208924b1eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1, P_2, P_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> are different</li></ul>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is called \"strong\" if there exists a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/1/1f18ce3bface8af8dde8251ea74f8b8b7410b555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{nx} + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>a. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa725c98dfe19f98809033755b801810bc298aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2013$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> is strong.\n</p><p>b. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is strong, determine the smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> (in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />) such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/1/1e1ae8401136621281547d90b8eaaa05b3c849a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^{my} + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/9/f2949376cf9667bec6117d164f65945d8a2c049f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^m$\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a parallelogram. Construct squares <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8ed969d6e2acb9d21eef69bc68f99077884fbc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC_1D_1, BCD_2A_2, CDA_3B_3, DAB_4C_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"310\" height=\"16\" /> on the outer side of the parallelogram. Construct a square having <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/3/633693b4353783afc825b25d17c5c08c7699fc8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_4D_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" /> as one of its sides and it is on the outer side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/e/c7ed5ac15e2ad1865f96491a5c4f9afeaa69b252.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB_4D_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" /> and call its center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/8/4d8aa423de2031c09aa06a1687767414dbb8120d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" />. Similarly do it for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/b/47b053988712600105b8c9baae73bd053612c2f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1A_2, D_2B_3, A_3C_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"142\" height=\"16\" /> to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/5/0552e28d2c565ae58e74f4df8a12a8d8f30d4ef4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_B, O_C, O_D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67a2255ef6c5de0dd6c91e44d7e781c6bd5302ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO_A = BO_B = CO_C = DO_D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"230\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be a set of positive integers. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is called \"balanced\" if [and only if] the number of 3-element subsets of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> whose elements add up to a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to the number of 3-element subsets of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> whose elements add up to not a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>a. Find a 9-element balanced set.\n</p><p>b. Prove that no set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa725c98dfe19f98809033755b801810bc298aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2013$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> elements can be balanced.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO\" title=\"2013 Indonesia MO\">2013 Indonesia MO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_Indonesia_MO\" title=\"2012 Indonesia MO\">2012 Indonesia MO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">7</a>